2.3 Three different products must not be conflated
The same array can inhabit different algebras. Its shape alone does not specify its multiplication. A
Boolean truth-table CM is generally neither invertible nor unitary. The all-ones truth table, the ordinary
identity matrix, and the convolution identity are three different objects. In particular, an equation such as
“𝑖 AND 𝑖” cannot be reinterpreted as convolution or gate composition without saying so.
